ed_at":"2026-10-07T14:25:42Z","closed_at":"2026-10-07T14:25:42Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.8.dev (current master)/ previous dev releases\n\n### System information\n\nWindows\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe diagnostic text displayed in the script editor hover tooltip can currently be selected with the mouse.\n\nThis appears to be unintended behavior. As discussed in [[#123310](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123310#pullrequestreview-5158246461)](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123310#pullrequestreview-5158246461), the diagnostic text in the tooltip should not be selectable. Since the tooltips does not work with shortcuts like Ctrl+C that closes the tooltip and there currently isn't a menu, selecting the text is not expected to be part of the interface.\n\n### Expected behavior\nThe diagnostic text should not be selectable. The tooltip should only provide the diagnostic information.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e57d61af-8bbb-4177-99cf-48260a4b1de6\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a GDScript file containing a warning or error.\n2. Hover over the warning or error to display the diagnostic tooltip.\n3. Click and drag across the diagnostic text.\n4. The text can be selected.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A\n\nThe issue can be reproduced in the script editor without a project-specific setup.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following